# The bulk fuzz corpus (hash-named entries from local `cargo fuzz run` sessions) is
# NOT committed — it is large and machine-generated. Only the hand-authored, valid
# `seed_*` files are tracked, so ClusterFuzzLite CI clones start from a real seed that
# reaches the decoder body (fuzz F1, 2026-07-02: the selector-gated targets
# multisend_decode / tx_erc20_parse_calldata never pass their 4-byte selector gate
# seedless, so their coverage-guided fuzzing was near-vacuous in CI).
*
!.gitignore
!*/
!*/seed_*
